## Why This Is Asked
This checks real-world ability to design multi-cloud patterns with clean module boundaries and governance.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform modules, provider aliases, multi-cloud strategy
- Environment backends and per-environment isolation
- CI gates, version constraints, governance for cloud support

## Code Example
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "aws"
  version = "~> 4.0"
  region  = var.aws_region
}
provider "google" {
  alias   = "google"
  version = "~> 4.0"
  project = var.gcp_project
}
provider "azurerm" {
  alias    = "azure"
  version  = "~> 3.0"
  features {}
}
module "monitors" {
  source       = "./modules/monitors"
  cloud_config = {
    aws   = { region = var.aws_region, enabled = true }
    gcp   = { region = var.gcp_region, enabled = true }
    azure = { region = var.azure_region, enabled = true }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-cloud drift in this pattern?
- How would you extend to add a new cloud while keeping tight approvals?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced Terraform design across multi-cloud per-tenant isolation, secret management, and policy enforcement. It also probes testing discipline and scalable module composition.

## Key Concepts

- Terraform provider aliases per tenant
- Tenant-scoped remote backends with encryption
- Vault-backed credentials retrieval
- Per-tenant RBAC and network segmentation
- Idempotence testing with Terratest
- Policy gates with OPA or Sentinel

## Code Example

```hcl
variable "tenants" {
  type = map(object({ cloud = string, region = string }))
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "tenant_${each.key}"
  region = var.tenants[each.key].region
  # fetch creds from Vault here
}

provider "azurerm" {
  alias   = "tenant_${each.key}"
  features = {}
}

terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    key = "state/${each.key}/terraform.tfstate"
    encryption = true
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evolve the design to support adding a new cloud to the tenant mix?
- How would you structure tests to run in parallel for many tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of per-env isolation, simple gating, and multi-provider setups for real-world tools like Databricks and Snowflake in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Env tagging across modules
- Per-env remote state backends
- Provider aliases for multi-environment isolation
- Lightweight CI gates for plan validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// backend snippet (per-env)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tf-state-bucket"
    key    = "env/dev/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "tf-locks-dev"
  }
}

// wrapper module outline
module "env_wrapper" {
  source = "./modules/env-wrapper"
  environment = var.environment
  tags = { Environment = var.environment }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend gates for Snowflake/DATABRICKS resources?
- How would you test the gating logic locally before CI?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-cloud infrastructure with consistent module boundaries, robust state management, and policy-driven gates, reflecting real-world enterprise needs.

## Key Concepts

- Terraform provider aliases and multiple backends
- Shared module design for multi-cloud resources
- Per-environment state isolation and plan gating
- Drift Detection and policy enforcement (OPA/Sentinel)
- CI/CD integration for plan-only gates

## Code Example

```hcl
# Minimal sketch illustrating two providers with aliases and a multi-env config
provider "aws" {
  region = var.aws_region
  alias  = "aws_prod"
}
provider "google" {
  project = var.gcp_project
  region  = var.gcp_region
  alias   = "gcp_prod"
}

module "messaging" {
  source = "./modules/messaging"
  config = {
    prod = {
      aws  = { region = "us-east-1" }
      gcp  = { project = "prod-project" }
    }
    staging = {
      aws  = { region = "us-west-2" }
      gcp  = { project = "staging-project" }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle secrets rotation across clouds in Terraform?
- What are the trade-offs of using Sentinel vs OPA for this gating scenario?
